          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Birth and Early Life</strong><br>\nKaiser Wilhelm II was born on January 27, 1859, in Potsdam, near Berlin. He was the eldest grandchild of Queen Victoria of the United Kingdom and related to many of Europe's reigning monarchs.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Ascension to the Throne</strong><br>\nWilhelm became Kaiser of Germany in 1888 following the death of his father, Emperor Frederick III. He quickly began to assert his influence on German government policy, emphasizing military buildup and a more aggressive foreign policy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Foreign Policy and Naval Expansion</strong><br>\nWilhelm's reign saw a significant expansion of the German Navy, aimed at rivaling Britain's Royal Navy. This naval race was a major cause of tension between Germany and Great Britain in the years leading up to World War I.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>World War I and Leadership</strong><br>\nAs Emperor during World War I, Wilhelm was the Supreme Warlord of the German forces. Early in the war, he encouraged his generals to pursue aggressive strategies in both Western and Eastern theaters.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Abdication and Exile</strong><br>\nFollowing Germany's deteriorating position in the war and the November Revolution at home, Wilhelm abdicated the throne on November 9, 1918. He went into exile in the Netherlands, where he spent the rest of his life.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Post-Abdication Period</strong><br>\nAfter his abdication, Wilhelm's political influence waned. His attempts to justify his and Germany's role in the war were seen in his memoirs, which garnered mixed receptions from the public and historians alike.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
